These files are UNMODIFIED. Do not edit them - the whole point is that the
plugin sees exactly the declarations NASSP was compiled against. To move to a
newer NASSP, re-vendor at the matching revision and rebuild; a mismatch here
does not fail to compile, it corrupts memory at runtime.

Only connector.cpp is compiled. The rest are headers it pulls in.
